extraStrings:
- type: en-US
  strings: &id001
    STR_INTEL_FILES: INTEL FILES
    STR_STORY_LOCK: Restricted
    STR_VIPER_INTERROGATION: Viper Interrogation
    STR_VIPER_INTERROGATION_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 1 of the trail. The prisoner is a Cobra trooper, a "Viper" in their own word for it: a former soldier with no papers, no unit patch and a rehearsed story. Scarlett
      broke the story in four days.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}He knows his cell, his sergeant and the colour of the trucks that bring the guns. He does not know who Cobra Commander is, and he is more afraid of Cobra
      than of us. That fear is the first useful thing we have learned about them.'
    STR_COBRA_ORDER_OF_BATTLE: Cobra Order of Battle
    STR_COBRA_ORDER_OF_BATTLE_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 2. From prisoners and recovered paperwork we can now draw Cobra the way it draws itself: troopers in cells of ten to fifteen, officers above the cells, pilots
      and drivers on the side, and a command nobody below the officers has seen.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Briefings from here on name what we are likely to face before we land. The Detention Block can be improved
      to hold more of them.'
    STR_VIPER_PILOT_INTERROGATION: Viper Pilot Interrogation
    STR_VIPER_PILOT_INTERROGATION_UFOPEDIA: Step 3. Cobra's pilots are better trained than its troopers and proud of it, which makes them talk. This one flew F.A.N.G. gyrocopters from a dirt strip he can
      describe down to the windsock.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}His flight school was military. Ours, he thinks. Our Skystriker crews will want to read what he says about how Cobra flies.
    STR_FANG_OPERATING_BASES: F.A.N.G. Operating Bases
    STR_FANG_OPERATING_BASES_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 4. The F.A.N.G. cannot fly far, so it never lives far from where it fights. Cobra keeps its gyrocopters at small airstrips: a hangar, a fuel bowser, a few men.
      Each one is a target we can find from the air and hit on the ground.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Airstrip raids are now possible wherever a strip is found.'
    STR_COBRA_OFFICER_INTERROGATION: Cobra Officer Interrogation
    STR_COBRA_OFFICER_INTERROGATION_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 5. The first Cobra officer to reach our cells. He wears the same blue as his men and a different look in his eye: he believes. He will not give us his
      commander.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}He gave us something better without meaning to. Officers move between cells by air, on a schedule, and he complained about the schedule.'
    STR_COBRA_FLIGHT_ROUTES: Cobra Flight Routes
    STR_COBRA_FLIGHT_ROUTES_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 6. Breaker has put the officer''s complaints against a year of civil air traffic, and Cobra''s cargo flights fall out of it: regular, unregistered, and always
      going somewhere quiet.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}A flight we know about is a flight we can follow home. A Signals Intelligence Center would let us listen to the rest.'
    STR_MEDI_VIPER_INTERROGATION: Medi-Viper Interrogation
    STR_MEDI_VIPER_INTERROGATION_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 7. Cobra''s field medic carries a kit that keeps wounded men fighting long after ours would be evacuated. Doc has been through all of it.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}The
      kit is good and we can build our own. Ask him about anything beyond the kit and he has nothing to say: whatever Cobra is planning for medicine, it has not reached the men in the field.'
    STR_ARASHIKAGE_INTERROGATION: Arashikage Interrogation
    STR_ARASHIKAGE_INTERROGATION_UFOPEDIA: Step 8. A ninja in Cobra's service, taken alive, which nobody here thought could be done. He gives his clan's name and nothing else for weeks.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Snake
      Eyes has been asked to read the transcripts. He has not said what he thinks of them.
    STR_ARASHIKAGE_CLAN_SECRETS: Arashikage Clan Secrets
    STR_ARASHIKAGE_CLAN_SECRETS_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 9. The Arashikage are a family of assassins older than Cobra and with no love for it. One of them works for Cobra Commander anyway, and the others call him
      by name: Storm Shadow.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}We know now where he trains and where he goes when the work is done.'
    STR_STORM_SHADOW_CAPTURED: Storm Shadow Captured
    STR_STORM_SHADOW_CAPTURED_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 10. Storm Shadow is in our cells. He does not resist and he does not explain himself. He asks for one thing: to speak with Snake Eyes.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}What
      he wants to say concerns the death of the Hard Master, the old head of his clan, and who really killed him.'
    STR_HARD_MASTERS_MURDER: The Hard Master's Murder
    STR_HARD_MASTERS_MURDER_UFOPEDIA: Storm Shadow joined Cobra to find the man who murdered his uncle, the Hard Master, and he believes that man is inside Cobra still. If we help him find the truth, he
      may stop being Cobra's weapon.
    STR_IRON_GRENADIER_INTERROGATION: Iron Grenadier Interrogation
    STR_IRON_GRENADIER_INTERROGATION_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 11. Destro''s own troops, in Destro''s own colours, fighting beside Cobra but answering to M.A.R.S. The prisoner is a professional and talks like one:
      about pay, contracts and shipping.'
    STR_MARS_SUPPLY_LINES: M.A.R.S. Supply Lines
    STR_MARS_SUPPLY_LINES_UFOPEDIA: Step 12. M.A.R.S. builds the weapons and Cobra fires them. The guns travel from M.A.R.S. factories by routes we can now name. Factory raids are possible wherever a factory
      is found.
    STR_MARS_FACTORY_RECORDS: M.A.R.S. Factory Records
    STR_MARS_FACTORY_RECORDS_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 13. Production records from a raided M.A.R.S. factory. Every order is signed off by the same man, and the signatures move: we can follow Destro from plant to
      plant.'
    STR_DESTRO_CAPTURED: Destro Captured
    STR_DESTRO_CAPTURED_UFOPEDIA: Step 14. James McCullen Destro XXIV, head of M.A.R.S., is our prisoner. He is courteous, untroubled and certain he will not be here long. He offers to talk business.
    STR_DESTROS_ARMS_LEDGER: Destro's Arms Ledger
    STR_DESTROS_ARMS_LEDGER_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 15. Destro''s private accounts: what M.A.R.S. has sold to Cobra, for how much, and what Cobra still owes. Cut those lines and Cobra''s money and guns both run
      short for a time.'
    STR_CRIMSON_GUARD_INTERROGATION: Crimson Guard Interrogation
    STR_CRIMSON_GUARD_INTERROGATION_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 16. The Crimson Guard are Cobra''s elite, and they live double lives: lawyers, accountants, a city councilman. This one had a law practice and a family
      in the suburbs.'
    STR_COBRAS_POLITICAL_FRONT: Cobra's Political Front
    STR_COBRAS_POLITICAL_FRONT_UFOPEDIA: Step 17. The Crimson Guard are only the visible part. Behind them is a network that buys elections, places people and gathers secrets, and it reports to the Baroness.
    STR_BARONESS_CAPTURED: The Baroness Captured
    STR_BARONESS_CAPTURED_UFOPEDIA: Step 18. Cobra's head of intelligence is in our cells. She has spent years looking for The Pit. Now she is in it, and she is still taking notes.
    STR_COBRA_INTELLIGENCE_NETWORK: Cobra Intelligence Network
    STR_COBRA_INTELLIGENCE_NETWORK_UFOPEDIA: Step 19. The Baroness's network, mapped. Her people report to regional hubs, and the hubs are Terror Dromes, including Dromes we did not know existed.
    STR_MINDBENDER_CAPTURED: Dr. Mindbender Captured
    STR_MINDBENDER_CAPTURED_UFOPEDIA: Step 20. Dr. Mindbender, Cobra's chief scientist. He is happy to talk about his work, at length, to anyone. Doc listens in shifts.
    STR_BRAINWAVE_BREAKTHROUGH: Brainwave Breakthrough
    STR_BRAINWAVE_BREAKTHROUGH_UFOPEDIA: Step 21. Mindbender's notes take our own brainwave work years forward, and they show us how to shield a mind from his.
    STR_TERROR_DROME_DATA_CORE: Terror Drome Data Core
    STR_TERROR_DROME_DATA_CORE_UFOPEDIA: 'Steps 22-23. The data core of a fallen Terror Drome: every order the Drome sent or received. Most of it is routine. Some of it comes from the top, and it is not
      about a war.'
    STR_COBRAS_TRUE_AGENDA: Cobra's True Agenda
    STR_COBRAS_TRUE_AGENDA_UFOPEDIA: Step 24. Put the Drome's orders beside Destro's ledger and the shape of it is plain. Cobra does not want to win a war. It wants to become a country.
    STR_COBRA_COMMANDERS_MOVEMENTS: Cobra Commander's Movements
    STR_COBRA_COMMANDERS_MOVEMENTS_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 25. Cobra Commander travels, and now we know how: which aircraft, which escorts, which sites he visits and how long he stays. He can be caught.'
    STR_COBRA_COMMANDER_CAPTURED: Cobra Commander Captured
    STR_COBRA_COMMANDER_CAPTURED_UFOPEDIA: Step 26. Cobra Commander is our prisoner. Under the hood is an ordinary man who once sold used cars, and who lost a brother and blamed the world for it. He will
      not tell us where Cobra will make its stand. His papers will.
    STR_LOCATION_COBRA_ISLAND: 'Location: Cobra Island'
    STR_LOCATION_COBRA_ISLAND_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 27. Cobra Island, in the Gulf of Mexico: built, armed and about to declare itself a nation.'
    STR_COBRA_ISLAND_OR_BUST: Cobra Island or Bust
    STR_COBRA_ISLAND_OR_BUST_UFOPEDIA: Step 28. Every Joe, every vehicle, every aircraft. Hawk has the plan. We go to Cobra Island.
    STR_BAT_FACTORY: B.A.T. Factory
    STR_BAT_FACTORY_UFOPEDIA: 'Step 29. The control chips in Cobra''s Battle Android Troopers and the M.A.R.S. supply lines lead to the same place: a plant where B.A.T.s are built by the hundred.'
    STR_VIPER_PILOT: Viper Pilot
    STR_COBRA_OFFICER: Cobra Officer
    STR_ARASHIKAGE: Arashikage
    STR_IRON_GRENADIER: Iron Grenadier
    STR_CRIMSON_GUARD: Crimson Guard
    STR_BARONESS: The Baroness
    STR_DR_MINDBENDER: Dr. Mindbender
- type: en-GB
  strings: *id001
